# Example iwd Wi-Fi profile (NOT loaded — documentation only).
#
# build/install.sh prompts for your SSID + passphrase at install time and writes
# the real profile to /var/lib/iwd/<SSID>.psk (chmod 600). iwd then auto-connects
# on boot, dhcpcd gets an IP + DNS, and the first-boot `nix profile install` can
# reach cache.nixos.org to fetch the desktop.
#
# The install default/suggestion is the workstation's network, "HOME_SA" — i.e.
# /var/lib/iwd/HOME_SA.psk would contain:
#
#   [Security]
#   Passphrase=your-wifi-password
#
#   [Settings]
#   AutoConnect=true
#
# Ethernet needs NO profile: dhcpcd.service handles the built-in e1000e NIC.
# To add/replace a network on a running system: `iwctl` (station … connect <ssid>).
